  "id": "interdisciplinary-approach",
  "term": "interdisciplinary approach",
  "definition": "An interdisciplinary approach is a way of studying or addressing a problem by bringing together multiple fields of expertise rather than relying on just one. In this source, it means combining medicine, philosophy, sociology, and psychology to examine sensitive communication about severe diagnoses, with philosophy playing a central role in shaping the study and interpreting its results.",
